# Pinned browser support floor. Reviewed & frozen: 2026-09-17.
#
# Do NOT use "defaults" here. "defaults" resolves against caniuse-lite's live
# global usage-share data, so a routine caniuse-lite bump (npm update, a
# dependency bot) can silently drop a browser our clients still use — this
# already happened once (commit f375b356 "fix old browsers support" had to
# re-add iOS/Safari >= 10 after "defaults" dropped them).
#
# Instead, every line below is an explicit version floor chosen deliberately.
# It only ever gets *raised*, and only on purpose (edit this file, bump the
# date above, note why). New browser releases above these floors are picked
# up automatically since there's no upper bound.
chrome >= 109
firefox >= 140
edge >= 146
safari >= 10
ios_saf >= 10
android >= 148
samsung >= 28
opera >= 127
op_mob >= 80